* The {{M|knockback}} distance calculation has two components — the first [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 1-3.png|21px]] {{Code|one-third intervals}} and the remaining [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 2-3.png|21px]] {{Code|two-thirds intervals}}.
** [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 1-3.png|21px]]
*** Knock units up to {{calc|trunc(1/3*v1)|v1={{#var:KnockInst}}}} instance, moving them a total of {{#vardefineecho:1stpart|{{calc|{{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}}*trunc(1/3*v1)|v1={{#var:KnockInst}}}}}} distance.
*** The affected units are knocked {{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}}-distance linearly per interval and is defined as:
**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|{{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}} × ( ⌊({{Quas}} × 20/3 × 1/3 )⌋ )}}
** [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 2-3.png|21px]]
*** For the remaining intervals ({{Code|i}}), {{#vardefineecho:2ndpart f|{{calc|ceil(2/3*v1)|v1={{#var:KnockInst}}}}}} instances, the affected units are moved {{Code|{{#vardefineecho:blast r|0.98}}}} exponentially from the per previous interval. {{#vardefine:blast a|0.98}}
*** Hence, the remaining intervals per level knocks the affected units by {{#vardefineecho:2ndpart|{{calc|{{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}}*{{#var:blast a}}*(1-{{#var:blast r}}^v1)/(1-{{#var:blast r}}) round1|v1={{#var:2ndpart f}}}}}}-distance and is defined as:
**** {{cf|expr}} {{Code|{{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}} × <nowiki>Σ_{n=1}^{i}</nowiki>({{#var:blast r}}^n)}}, where {{Code|i}} is the remaining intervals.

* Therefore, the total {{M|knockback}} distance is defined as:
** [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 1-3.png|21px]] + [[File:Dota2 Invoker Deafening Blast 2-3.png|21px]] ≈ {{calc|v1+v2 round0|v1={{#var:1stpart}}|v2={{#var:2ndpart}}}}
** In short, the knockback starts from a {{#expr:{{#var:Deafening Blast basic2}}/({{G|tick rate}} round2)}}-speed and decreases exponentially.

